{# The concurrency section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# concurrency findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text) so #}
{# each template passes its own heading text. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{% macro concurrency_section(findings, heading) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The following concurrency constructs were recognized in this function by static
analysis. Where a finding is credible, express the synchronization with the
suggested Rust type instead of transliterating the manual lock/unlock or
spawn/join calls:

{% for finding in findings %}
- **{{ finding.suggestion|safe }}** ({{ finding.kind }} construct, confidence {{ finding.confidence }})
  Evidence: `{{ finding.evidence|safe }}`
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
